  "upstream": {
    "FieldTrip": "FieldTrip template/electrode/standard_1005.elc: 10-05 positions constructed by Robert Oostenveld (Oostenveld and Praamstra 2001, The five percent electrode system for high-resolution EEG and ERP measurements), in millimeters in Montreal Neurological Institute (MNI) coordinates on FieldTrip's template head (Colin27). The FieldTrip repository is GPL-3.0 and its website CC BY-SA 4.0; neither states a license for the template electrode files. MNE-Python ships the file under its BSD-3-Clause license.",
    "EGI": "Electrical Geodesics, Inc. (EGI) HydroCel Geodesic Sensor Net layouts. FieldTrip states its template/electrode/GSN-HydroCel-*.sfp files were downloaded from the EGI FTP server, and MNE-Python's montage README says its GSN-HydroCel files are taken from FieldTrip. MNE's files hold the same numbers as FieldTrip's (FieldTrip names the 64 and 65 nets without _1.0); the bytes differ in whitespace. No license is stated for the layouts by EGI or FieldTrip; MNE-Python ships them under BSD-3-Clause.",
    "BioSemi": "BioSemi head cap layouts (ABC labels, A1 to H32), as spherical angles in MNE-Python's biosemi*.txt. MNE's montage README does not name their origin. BioSemi publishes the position coordinates of its standard head caps (biosemi.com/download/Cap_coords_all.xls, linked from biosemi.com/headcap.htm) with no license statement; its 16, 32 and 64 channel sheets list the same 10-20 names and angles as MNE's biosemi16/32/64.txt, in the same order (spreadsheet SHA-256 38304148957c86b16622a7511c972f268ecbe2a7da2288edd3d59718ab82e2fa); the 128, 160 and 256 channel sheets were not compared. MNE-Python ships the files under BSD-3-Clause."
  },
